## Working loop

1. At task start, run only `git worktree list --porcelain`. Before planning, list open Milestones and Issues, then search open and closed Issues with two to four concrete terms (at most 20 candidates per query); read the body, comments, and linked pull requests of credible matches.
2. Before creating a work item, summarize prior decisions; record each relevant `#N` as preserved, superseded, or rejected, or the bounded queries when none exist. Update `docs/adr/` when a user confirms a durable constraint. Never store a transcript, promote an inference to a decision, or silently reverse an earlier decision.
3. Use the checked-in Issue forms and pull request template. Open or select one Issue before editing and use its acceptance criteria as scope. Titles use 12-80 ASCII characters, at least three words, no type prefix, and no trailing period. Set one native Type and an assignee (`--assignee @me`){% if 'milestones' in lifecycle %} and the Milestone; every resolving PR inherits the Issue's Milestone{% endif %}. Edit Issue bodies with `.csarc/scripts/gh-issue-edit`, which warns before an edit invalidates an approval.
4. If new work exceeds the Issue, open a separate Issue instead of widening the branch{% if 'milestones' in lifecycle %}; work discovered inside a Milestone stays in that Milestone unless it spans Milestones, is an urgent production fix, or comes from an unrelated external report{% endif %}.
5. Every work Issue carries the `#### 風險與控制` block. Before Ready, the pull request's `## Requirement evidence` maps every acceptance criterion (AC1..ACn) and risk ID to exact-head evidence, a reasoned `manual:` link, or a visible `accepted: <reason>` for a risk; never invent evidence or use `R0` or `accepted:` to hide a real risk.
6. Start from {% if 'milestones' in lifecycle %}the Milestone's `dev/m<milestone>-short-slug` branch, or {% endif %}current `main`. Use `.csarc/scripts/gh-issue-develop <issue> --base <base> --name type/<issue-number>-short-slug`; its `--repair-from` works only before a pull request exists. GitHub closes a pull request whose head branch is renamed or whose base branch is deleted, so never rename or delete an open PR's head, and retarget a stacked PR before its base branch is merged.
7. Inspect nearby code and tests, make the smallest coherent change, preserve unrelated work, and add the narrowest regression test that proves non-trivial behavior.
8. {% if verification_mode == 'local' %}After the candidate is committed and clean, run `./.csarc/scripts/verify-fast` once; a later tree or base change requires one new run.{% else %}Rely on the hosted `verify` check for the risk-owned suite; do not rerun the aggregate suite solely because the hosted plan selects `fast` or `full`.{% endif %}
9. Check every acceptance and checklist box only with real evidence, all at once before the push meant to satisfy the closing keyword; keep the pull request Draft until then.
10. Serialize the finalization window per destination base: a worker reports `READY_TO_FINALIZE` with its Issue, branch, head, and base and yields; independent sessions run `.csarc/scripts/finalization-queue announce --issue <N> --base <branch>` and proceed only when `status` reports `ready`. The queue is advisory and never grants authorization.
{% if release_ownership == 'csarc-owned' %}11. For release-worthy work, update from the destination base, run `python3 .csarc/scripts/release_policy.py prepare-candidate --sha HEAD --phase <beta|stable>` ({% if 'milestones' in lifecycle %}`beta` for Milestone work, {% endif %}`stable` otherwise), and commit only the version surfaces and CHANGELOG as the final commit of the same pull request. Never defer version creation to a later pull request.
{% else %}11. This repository has no CSARC release step; never create version tags or Releases.
{% endif %}12. Create the pull request as Draft with `.csarc/scripts/pr_lifecycle.py create`. Before any later Ready/Draft, authorization, metadata, or merge write, acquire the remote lease and use `.csarc/scripts/pr_lifecycle.py`; otherwise stay read-only.
13. After merge, confirm the exact head merged, the Issue reached its expected state, the release decision completed, and the branch and lease were removed. Then run `./.csarc/scripts/cleanup-worktrees --apply --worktree <path> origin/<base>` from another checkout and `.csarc/scripts/finalization-queue leave --issue <N>`; never remove another task's or a dirty, locked, or unmerged worktree.
14. Report `WAITING` with the exact external condition, `BLOCKED` only when no safe progress remains, and `DONE` only after step 13. A worker then reports `ARCHIVE_READY` and yields.

Never push directly to an integration branch, invent evidence, create release tags by hand, or bypass the linked governance policy. Use local storage for worktrees; if given a cloud-synced path, switch to a local checkout and preserve changes.

## Commands

{% if "python" in languages %}- Python setup: `uv sync --locked`; iterate with `uv run ruff check <paths>`, `uv run ty check`, and `uv run pytest <test-path>`.
{% endif %}{% if "typescript" in languages %}- TypeScript setup: `corepack enable && pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`; iterate with `pnpm exec biome check <paths>`, `pnpm exec tsc --noEmit`, and `pnpm exec vitest run <test-path>`.
{% endif %}{% if "rust" in languages %}- Rust setup: `rustup show && cargo fetch --locked` (Linux/WSL2 also needs a C linker such as `build-essential`); iterate with `cargo fmt --all -- --check`, `cargo clippy --locked --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`, and `cargo test --locked`.
{% endif %}{% if "go" in languages %}- Go setup: install Go 1.27.1, keep `GOTOOLCHAIN=local`, and run `go mod download`; iterate with `gofmt -l <paths>`, `go vet ./...`, and `go test ./...`.
{% endif %}{% if not languages %}- No language toolchain install is required.
{% endif %}{% if documentation_mode == 'template-and-content' %}- Site source check: `./.csarc/scripts/build-repo-site --check`.
{% endif %}- Final verification: {% if verification_mode == 'local' %}`./.csarc/scripts/verify-fast` once after committing; it promotes full-risk work to `./.csarc/scripts/verify`.{% else %}the hosted `verify` check; `./.csarc/scripts/check-trusted-verification <head-sha> --github-repo <owner/repo>` reads its evidence.{% endif %}
{% if copilot_review == 'allowed' %}- Copilot review: `python3 .csarc/scripts/review_gate.py status --repo <owner/repo> --pr <N>` lists findings and unresolved threads on the current head; fix, push, resolve, and repeat until clean, or obtain a maintainer approval of the exact head.
{% endif %}{% if release_ownership == 'csarc-owned' %}- Release execution: after merge, `.csarc/scripts/publish-release` publishes the reviewed candidate; never create a replacement version pull request or tag by hand.
{% endif %}{% if 'milestones' in lifecycle %}- Milestone preflight: `python3 .csarc/scripts/sync_milestone_state.py preflight --repo <repo> --milestone <N>`; see `.csarc/docs/milestone-description.md`.
{% endif %}
## Boundaries and safety

{% if languages %}- Product code and tests belong to this project; template updates must not overwrite them. Do not hand-edit lockfiles.
{% endif %}- Keep third-party GitHub Actions pinned to full commit SHAs. Do not create a separate GitHub repository for testing. Comments in source code must be written in English.
- Never extract or persist `gh auth token`, treat a permission error as proof of a capability, or claim a skipped control succeeded.
- Never commit secrets, tokens, private keys, or populated `.env` files. Review `.csarc/scripts/apply-repository-settings.sh plan` before `apply`; do not operate production or external infrastructure without explicit authorization.
- Review dependency, workflow-permission, secret-handling, and public-interface changes as security-sensitive, and require tests for behavior changes.
- Add a nested `AGENTS.md` only when a subtree has genuinely different commands, ownership, or safety boundaries.
